title: SPIR-V Specification
author: John Kessenich, Google
author: Boaz Ouriel, Intel
author: Raun Krisch, Intel
author: Victor Lomüller, Codeplay
changes:

=== Changes from Version 1.6, Revision 3

- Reserve enumerants for:
 * SPV_KHR_float_controls2
 * SPV_KHR_maximal_reconvergence
 * SPV_KHR_quad_control
 * SPV_KHR_relaxed_extended_instruction
 * SPV_EXT_replicated_composites
 * SPV_INTEL_fpga_cluster_attributes
 * SPV_INTEL_masked_gather_scatter
 * SPV_INTEL_maximum_registers
 * SPV_QCOM_image_processing2
 * SPV_NV_shader_atomic_fp16_vector
 * SPV_NV_raw_access_chains

- Other changes from public headers
 * Enforce Core, KHR, EXT, Vendor ordering conventions for aliased names
 * Added <<Source_Language, source languages>> Zig
 * Removed the *Kernel* enabling capability from <<Image_Channel_Order, Image Channel Order>> and <<Image_Channel_Data_Type, Image Channel Data Type>>.

- Fix Khronos SPIR-V Issues:
 * #638: Clarify that most <<Execution_Mode,execution modes>> must be applied at most once to a given <<EntryPoint,entry point>>.
 * #766: Clarify the texel value type for the *ZeroExtend* and *SignExtend*
         <<Image_Operands,image operands>>.
 * #724: Clarify that the <<Storage_Class,storage class>> must match
         when performing an <<OpBitcast,*OpBitcast*>> between two <<OpTypePointer,*OpTypePointer*>>.
         Clarify that the behavior is undefined when using the result of a bit cast between a scalar
         and a pointer (<<OpBitcast,*OpBitcast*>> and <<OpConvertUToPtr,*OpConvertUToPtr*>>) if
         the <<Storage_Class,storage class>> scalar.
 * Add optional operand for <<OpTypeFloat, *OpTypeFloat*>> to specify bit pattern of values.
   Clarify that OpFConvert operates on different types not just width.
   Clarify the following uses IEEE 754 floating-points:
     `OpQuantizeToF16`, <<Image_Operands, Image Operands>> taking <<Floating,_floating-point type_>> operands,
     *VecTypeHint*, *DenormPreserve*, *DenormFlushToZero*, *SignedZeroInfNanPreserve*, *RoundingModeRTE* and *RoundingModeRTZ* <<Execution_Mode, execution mode>>,
     <<Derivative, Derivative instructions>>, *Float16Buffer*, *Float16* and *Int64* <<Capability, capabilities>>.
   Clarify that <<OpIsNan, *OpIsNan*>>, <<OpIsInf, *OpIsInf*>>, <<OpIsFinite, *OpIsFinite*>>, <<OpOrdered, *OpOrdered*>> and <<OpUnordered, *OpUnordered*>> results depends on the floating-point encoding.
 * #767: Rework the *Function* <<Storage_Class,Storage Class>> definition.
         Clarify the memory is visible across all functions and not just the declaring function.
         Clarify that an <<OpVariable,*OpVariable*>> with a *Function* <<Storage_Class,Storage Class>> is only allocated from its declaration until reaching a <<FunctionTermination, function termination instruction>>.
